# SeePat — local environment.
#
# This file is COMMITTED on purpose: it holds defaults, never secrets. There is
# no server, no payment gateway and no AI service in this repository, so no key
# exists to leak. The moment one does, it goes in .env.local (git-ignored, and
# it overrides this file) — never here.
#
# Every variable is explained in full in .env.example, which is the file to
# read or copy when setting a machine up from scratch.

# The origin the app is deployed to, with NO trailing slash. Used only to build
# absolute OG/Twitter card URLs in index.html (%VITE_SITE_URL%/og-image.png).
# Empty is a valid, deliberate state: the tags then fall back to root-relative
# paths, which every crawler except Facebook resolves correctly. Set it before
# a production build.
#   production: https://seepat.ph
VITE_SITE_URL=
